# THE SUMP — a big, lumbering, formerly human brute for the FPS roster.
#
# AUTHORED FROM PROSE (PRDs/001-sump-body-horror-brute.md). There is no
# reference mesh and no reference plate — the owner explicitly wants an
# original interpretation from the prose — so, exactly as gnasher.blob
# records of itself, blob:measure and blob:rings do not apply and NO number
# below is "measured". Every one is a design decision; the comment on each
# non-obvious number says WHY (or names the prose beat it serves, or the
# turntable round that forced it).
#
# WHO IT IS. A tragic living prosthetic effect: flesh stretched around a body
# that has grown in the wrong directions. The weight of a Quake 1 ogre,
# Dead Space's anatomical disruption, Basket Case's grotesque. NOT an athlete,
# NOT a balloon: heavy, grounded, and asymmetrical in the OUTLINE, not just
# the surface colour.
#
# ROUND 2 (turntable r1): the first body validated clean and still read as a
# SCRAWNY humanoid on sticks — thin limbs, a slab torso, ball-jointed legs,
# tiny feet. Every mass below was fattened 15-30%, the torso blends were
# raised so the masses read as ONE sagging column rather than stacked balls,
# the legs took a wider stance (side 0.17) under the extra girth, and the
# belly was carried FORWARD (z 0.19) so it hangs under the chest, ahead of
# the thighs, instead of swallowing them.
#
# THE FIVE BEATS, made concrete:
#   1. HUNCHED MASS. ~2.2 m of body carried on two SHORT legs (hip line 1.05,
#      48% of height). The spine chain leans the shoulders well ahead of the
#      hips; the neck disappears into a raised back, so there is no visible
#      neck column. The yoke spans ~0.72 m across the shoulders — the widest
#      thing above the hips.
#   2. THE HANGING BELLY. A heavy sag carried FORWARD of the thighs: bottom
#      ~0.75 (below the crotch at 0.90, well above the knee at 0.555), front
#      surface at z ~0.45 level with the hunched chest — the profile reads as
#      a belly leading, thighs behind (pinned in sump-blob.test.ts).
#   3. UNEQUAL ARMS. The +x arm has overgrown into a dragging, knotted
#      striking limb: a huge deltoid, crooked shaft, elbow and wrist knots,
#      and an oversized fist that hangs just above the knee line (fist bottom
#      ~0.75 vs the human hand at ~1.05). The -x arm stays recognizably human
#      — thick, misshapen, human length. Both arms ride the same (symmetric)
#      rig bones — the mirror block — and the asymmetry is authored in FLESH
#      with `side=l` / `side=r` prims (in this rig `.l` bones land at +x, the
#      same side as the torso offsets that carry the second face — the two
#      must agree), so the gait/carry rig keeps working unchanged. The
#      outline difference is the point: one arm is a limb, the other a verdict.
#   4. THE FACE IN THE SHOULDER. The defining horror: a second, INCOMPLETE
#      face compressed into the swollen shoulder above the overgrown arm — a
#      collapsed brow (one end drooping), ONE recessed eye, and a crooked
#      mouth-like fold (two stepped grooves). Attached anatomy on the torso
#      cluster, not a separate head and not a decal; it must read at
#      inspection distance without out-competing the main face, so it is
#      smaller, dimmer, and has no teeth.
#   5. THE SMALL UGLY MAIN FACE. Low heavy brow, crushed nose, one sagging
#      cheek (the -x side), an off-centre heavy jaw with a few irregular
#      teeth behind a mostly CLOSED dark mouth line. Dim recognition and
#      discomfort — deliberately NOT a giant toothy grin.
#
# PALETTE. Sickly, desaturated, thick and dull: waxy grey-beige base, bruised
# plum mottle (hue-different from the base, so it reads as bruising IN the
# skin), raw red only where tissue is exposed. wetness is LOW — highlights
# are reserved for the mouth and one irritated seam, which carry their own
# `gloss=`. NOTHING glows on this character: the eyes are small, inset, and
# non-glowing (pinned as zero glow prims in the test).
#
# LANDMARKS, NOT TUMORS. The back and shoulder carry a few strong stretched
# ridges and compressed folds (five pieces) that explain where the extra mass
# came from. No fields of boils, no spikes.
#
# NOT THE OTHER ROSTER HEAVIES. No maw (gnasher), no ball body (bloatmaw),
# no machinery (cyberdemon), no wings/tail (gargoyle), no horns (minotaur —
# abandoned, but the silhouette lesson stands).
model sump
  # Declared standing height = the crown as authored (2.19 measured). Bottom
  # of the PRD's 2.2-2.5 m band: the hunch IS the crouch that reduces the
  # apparent height, so the silhouette reads heavier than tall.
  height 2.20
  # Declared, not implied: humanoid knees (slight forward fold), verified by
  # checkStance. Omitting the line would mean "not checked", not "humanoid".
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # Hip line at 1.05 (root 0.90 + len 0.15; children attach at the TAIL).
  # SHORT load-bearing legs on a 2.2 m body: the pelvis len restores the
  # crotch-to-hip segment, as gnasher.blob does.
  root pelvis at 0.90 len=0.15

  # The hunched chain. PITCH IS PER-BONE (absolute from vertical), not
  # accumulated — the r2 chain said 18/16/34/24 and leaned only 24 deg at the
  # skull, so the head sat ON TOP of the shoulder ball and the torso read
  # upright. Now: 26+24 puts the shoulder line ahead of the hips, and the
  # steep neck/skull (38/26) shove the head forward out of the raised back —
  # the small head leads, the big body looms behind it. The skull stops at 26
  # (a first draft at 40 aimed the face at the FLOOR: no camera angle, in the
  # lab or in-game, could see the face) — enough down-tilt to glower, not
  # enough to hide it.
  bone spine parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=26 len=0.46
  bone chest parent=spine  dir=up pitch=24 len=0.42
  bone neck  parent=chest  dir=up pitch=38 len=0.12
  bone skull parent=neck   dir=up pitch=26 len=0.19

  mirror
    # Shoulder yoke. tilt=10 lifts the clavicle into the trap slope; the 0.26
    # reach plus the flesh yoke mass (not the bone) is what makes the
    # shoulder line read as enormous.
    bone clavicle parent=chest    dir=side tilt=10 len=0.26
    # Human-scale arm bones on BOTH sides — the overgrown +x arm is authored
    # in flesh (see the body block), so the rig poses both arms identically
    # and the silhouette carries the asymmetry. tilt=24 splays both arms out
    # under the yoke: a heavy brute's arms rest ON the lats, and the elbow
    # needs the air (two rounds bought this number — see the upper-arm line).
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down pitch=10 tilt=24 len=0.34
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down pitch=8  tilt=5  len=0.32
    bone hand     parent=foreArm  dir=down pitch=12         len=0.13
    # Legs: near-vertical thigh, slight forward knee fold (humanoid —
    # checkStance verifies the knee sits in FRONT of the hip->ankle line; a
    # first draft at thigh 5 / shin 6 folded 4 mm BACKWARD), then a short
    # foot bone pitched down-forward to a broad flat pad. side=0.17: the wide
    # pillar stance the r2 girth needs — thin legs under a hanging belly
    # merged with it; these clear it.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down pitch=7  tilt=4 side=0.17 len=0.50
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down pitch=2            len=0.44
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=down pitch=58           len=0.14
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — one sagging hunched column, NOT a stack of balls: the r1
  # turntable read the r1 masses as separate lumps, so r2 fattens each mass
  # AND raises the blends (0.024-0.030) until neighbours overlap into flesh.
  # Kept narrower in x than the yoke: the arms take their air from the chest
  # width, and the brute's mass reads in DEPTH and shoulder line (the
  # gnasher/goblin lesson).
  # ============================================================
  # Haunch: the seat the short legs root into, deep enough to carry the
  # profile under the belly.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.35 r=0.215 wide=1.15 tall=1.05 deep=1.20 blend=0.024
  # Lower spine mass: fills the y band between haunch and chest so the torso
  # is ONE column (a first draft left an 8 cm gap at y ~1.38 and the legs
  # failed their fuse probe through it).
  blob torso on spine  at=0.30 r=0.235 wide=1.00 tall=1.10 deep=1.10 blend=0.024
  # Upper belly: bridges the waist->chest seam at z ~0.12 (the fuse probe
  # threaded exactly between the two ellipsoids there) and reads as the
  # diaphragm mass under the hunched chest.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.76 offset=(0,-0.005,-0.030) r=0.225 wide=1.05 tall=1.00 deep=1.05 blend=0.026
  # Chest barrel: the biggest mass, deep in z — the hunch reads in profile.
  # Narrow in x (semi 0.306) and trimmed in z for the overgrown arm's elbow
  # (two rounds bought this number — see the upper-arm line).
  blob torso on chest  at=0.55 r=0.255 wide=1.20 tall=1.15 deep=1.10 blend=0.026 core
  # Shoulder yoke: the enormous hunched shoulder line — semi-x 0.361, the
  # widest span on the body (~0.72 m), what the hunched read stands on.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.95 r=0.195 wide=1.85 tall=0.80 deep=1.10 blend=0.020
  # RAISED BACK: the hump behind/above the yoke that swallows the neck. Pushed
  # to -z and up so the profile shows a continuous back line into the skull.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.80 offset=(0,0.050,-0.155) r=0.215 wide=1.35 tall=0.95 deep=1.05 blend=0.026
  # HANGING BELLY: deep in +z and dropped — carried FORWARD of the thighs
  # (offset z 0.19), which is what lets it hang low without swallowing them.
  # Bottom ~0.78, below the crotch (0.90), well above the knee (0.555);
  # pinned as a band in sump-blob.test.ts.
  blob torso on spine  at=0.02 offset=(0,-0.005,0.190) r=0.235 wide=1.00 tall=1.00 deep=1.05 blend=0.028
  # Belly sag: the underside roll, where the weight gathers above the crotch.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.30 offset=(0,0.015,0.175) r=0.205 wide=1.00 tall=0.80 deep=1.10 blend=0.026
  # Glutes: heavy masses directly OVER the hip joints — anatomically where a
  # brute carries the short legs, and structurally the weld that lets the
  # thigh fuse past the haunch's x-edge (the legs' fuse probe failed by
  # 7 mm without them).
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.42 offset=(0.150,0.020,-0.030) r=0.135 wide=1.05 tall=1.00 deep=1.15 blend=0.022 both
  # SWOLLEN +x SHOULDER: the host mass for the second face. Sits high on the
  # shoulder, proud of the yoke — the asymmetry that makes that side read
  # heavier before you even find the face.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.92 offset=(0.215,0.045,0.015) r=0.215 wide=1.30 tall=0.78 deep=0.72 blend=0.022

  # ============================================================
  # THE SECOND FACE — compressed into the swollen shoulder above the
  # overgrown arm. Incomplete ON PURPOSE: collapsed brow, ONE recessed eye,
  # a crooked mouth-like fold. No teeth, no second jaw — it is another person
  # being ABSORBED, suggested rather than stated, and it must not out-shout
  # the main face. All on the torso cluster (attached anatomy, not a head).
  # PLACEMENT: every offset below was computed by ray-marching the HOST
  # mass's own field along +z at the feature's (x, y) — three rounds of hand
  # arithmetic placed these features floating ahead of the shoulder, buried
  # inside it, or under a lid that had grown over the whole eye. Don't hand-
  # place features on a pitched bone; march the host surface and paste.
  # ============================================================
  # Collapsed brow: a shelf over the eye whose far end DROOPS (negative tip
  # y) — the fold of a brow that caved. Chamfer keeps the crease.
  bar torso on chest from=0.92 to=0.92 offset=(0.360,0.185,0.104) tip=(-0.190,-0.050,-0.005) r=0.052 wide=1.10 tall=0.50 deep=0.80 blend=0.006 chamfer
  # Eye socket: a dark crater (the bloatmaw idiom — a painted pit so the small
  # eye reads OUT of shadow rather than as a speck on flesh). Its front sits
  # ~0.03 proud of the swelling so it owns its pixels.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.92 offset=(0.330,0.112,0.192) r=0.070 wide=1.00 tall=0.90 deep=0.40 blend=0.006 color=241511
  # The recessed eye itself: small, dim, wet, NOT glowing, and set BEHIND the
  # socket's rim so it reads as sunk into the swelling.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.92 offset=(0.330,0.110,0.200) r=0.028 wide=0.90 tall=0.90 deep=0.55 blend=0.004 color=e0d6c2 gloss=0.80
  # Lid fold: a flesh blob rising over the eye's top half — half-closed, tired.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.92 offset=(0.330,0.142,0.170) r=0.050 wide=1.05 tall=0.55 deep=0.70 blend=0.006
  # The crooked mouth-like fold: TWO stepped groove segments (a short branch
  # dropping off the main crease) — a fold that ALMOST makes a mouth.
  # Groove arithmetic (reference.md): real half-width = width / min(scale).
  # Main crease: r=0.030, wide=2.0 tall=0.05 deep=0.70 -> min 0.05; a 4 mm
  # half-width band is width = 0.004 x 0.05 = 0.0002. depth 2.5 mm is the cut.
  groove torso on chest at=0.92 r=0.040 wide=2.00 tall=0.05 deep=0.70 depth=0.0050 width=0.00027 offset=(0.325,0.070,0.170) tip=(-0.110,-0.012,-0.005)
  # Branch: shorter, stepping DOWN toward the cheek, the "crooked" in the fold.
  groove torso on chest at=0.92 r=0.030 wide=1.40 tall=0.05 deep=0.60 depth=0.0040 width=0.00027 offset=(0.258,0.054,0.178) tip=(-0.055,0.014,-0.006)
  # Mouth aperture: a small dark mass at the main fold's inner end, so the
  # fold reads as a slightly parted mouth rather than a scratch (the
  # bloatmaw darks-own-their-pixels rule: the aperture protrudes past the
  # swelling and paints near-black with a wet catch).
  blob torso on chest  at=0.92 offset=(0.295,0.087,0.166) r=0.026 wide=1.40 tall=0.70 deep=0.50 blend=0.005 color=1a0b0a gloss=0.40

  # ============================================================
  # BACK AND SHOULDER LANDMARKS — stretched ridges and compressed folds, a
  # few strong pieces that explain the extra mass. Restrained by design.
  # ============================================================
  # Stretched ridge, upper back: a long low diagonal bar, chamfered so it
  # keeps a crease — skin stretched OVER the growth.
  bar torso on spine from=0.60 to=0.60 offset=(-0.120,0.105,-0.180) tip=(0.235,-0.055,0.015) bend=(0,-0.025,0.020) r=0.028 wide=1.10 tall=0.55 deep=0.85 blend=0.006 chamfer
  # Stretched ridge, lower: the counter-diagonal, so the back reads as pulled
  # from two directions, not stamped.
  bar torso on spine from=0.25 to=0.25 offset=(0.125,0.060,-0.190) tip=(-0.220,-0.040,0.015) r=0.026 wide=1.00 tall=0.50 deep=0.80 blend=0.006 chamfer
  # Belly crease: the horizontal fold where the overhang turns under. Painted
  # bruised plum — the PRD puts bruising in the compressed folds.
  bar torso on spine from=0.05 to=0.05 offset=(0,-0.245,0.215) tip=(0.155,0.020,0.030) r=0.030 wide=1.15 tall=0.50 deep=0.80 blend=0.005 chamfer color=4a3244
  # +x flank fold: a vertical compressed roll where belly meets hip.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.42 offset=(0.195,0.045,0.120) r=0.075 wide=0.55 tall=1.05 deep=1.00 blend=0.008 color=443040
  # Irritated seam: ONE raw-red line where the fold weeps, with the only
  # strong gloss on the body — the PRD's "wet highlights reserved for the
  # mouth and a few irritated seams".
  bar torso on pelvis from=0.40 to=0.40 offset=(0.140,-0.075,0.185) tip=(-0.010,-0.075,0.010) r=0.015 wide=0.70 tall=0.40 deep=0.50 blend=0.004 color=6e211d gloss=0.40

  # ============================================================
  # NECK + HEAD — small and ugly, shoved forward out of the raised back.
  # All prims (no reference mesh to bake; the painted-face road is the
  # documented failure), so the face block below is a nub. The head is
  # SMALL on the body (~0.21 m cranium on 2.2 m) — that ratio is the beat.
  # Order matters: masses first, then the mouth interior, teeth, and eyes
  # last so the brow still shadows them.
  # ============================================================
  # Neck: a short thick column, mostly SWALLOWED by the raised back and yoke;
  # it exists to fuse the head into the torso without a gap.
  bar head on neck from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.105 deep=0.95 blend=0.012
  # Cranium: the small dome.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 r=0.115 wide=0.95 tall=1.00 deep=1.05 blend=0.008 core
  # Low heavy brow: a wide low shelf, PLUS a droopier second piece over the
  # +x eye — the asymmetric scowl of dim recognition.
  bar head on skull from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0,0.091,0.082) tip=(0,-0.008,0.028) r=0.030 wide=1.45 tall=0.50 deep=0.70 blend=0.005 chamfer
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.052,0.078,0.056) r=0.046 wide=0.90 tall=0.60 deep=0.75 blend=0.005
  # Crushed nose: squat, wide, flattened, nudged off centre — it reads as
  # having been broken more than once.
  blob head on skull at=0.44 offset=(0.010,-0.009,0.144) r=0.040 wide=1.35 tall=0.75 deep=0.80 blend=0.005
  # Sagging cheek: the -x side, a drooping jowl pulled down by the same
  # gravity as everything else.
  blob head on skull at=0.44 offset=(-0.062,-0.049,0.041) r=0.052 wide=0.90 tall=1.20 deep=0.90 blend=0.008
  # Heavy jaw: off-centre (+x) and jutted — the bite is wrong, which is part
  # of the discomfort.
  blob head on skull at=0.26 offset=(0.018,-0.075,0.066) r=0.078 wide=1.05 tall=0.85 deep=1.05 blend=0.008
  # Chin mass: pushes the jut further forward under the mouth line.
  blob head on skull at=0.22 offset=(0.024,-0.102,0.112) r=0.049 wide=1.00 tall=0.80 deep=0.90 blend=0.006
  # Upper-lip ridge: flesh, proud of the jaw above the mouth line, so the
  # mouth is a crease BETWEEN reliefs, not paint on a flat.
  bar head on skull from=0.32 to=0.32 offset=(0.012,-0.021,0.115) tip=(0.052,0.006,-0.012) r=0.011 wide=1.30 tall=0.40 deep=0.50 blend=0.003
  # MOUTH: a mostly closed, slightly parted dark line, crooked (the tip makes
  # it slant down toward the sagging side), WET — one of the reserved glosses.
  # It sits BETWEEN the lip ridge above and the jaw mass below.
  bar head on skull from=0.32 to=0.32 offset=(0.012,-0.033,0.088) tip=(0.052,-0.010,-0.014) r=0.012 wide=1.35 tall=0.45 deep=0.50 blend=0.003 color=200a08 gloss=0.60
  # Mouth corner: closes the aperture at the +x end so the line reads as a
  # mouth, not a slash.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.052,-0.029,0.066) r=0.017 wide=0.90 tall=0.90 deep=0.80 blend=0.004 color=200a08
  # A FEW irregular teeth, small, breaking the dark line — not a grin. Sizes
  # and spacing deliberately uneven; dull ivory, low gloss. Rooted IN the
  # mouth line's own mass (a first draft rooted them on the jaw's front
  # surface and stranded 2 cm clear of it).
  blob head on skull at=0.31 offset=(0.030,-0.039,0.104) r=0.0085 r2=0.004 blend=0.002 tip=(0.002,-0.014,-0.002) color=cfc3a4 gloss=0.25
  blob head on skull at=0.33 offset=(-0.004,-0.044,0.100) r=0.0105 r2=0.004 blend=0.002 tip=(-0.003,-0.017,-0.002) color=c8bb9c gloss=0.25
  blob head on skull at=0.33 offset=(-0.022,-0.043,0.093) r=0.0075 r2=0.003 blend=0.002 tip=(0.001,-0.012,-0.003) color=cfc3a4 gloss=0.25
  # EYES: small, inset, uneven, NON-GLOWING. Dark socket craters first (the
  # bloatmaw idiom), then small wet eyeballs RECESSED behind the rim, then
  # heavy lid folds that half-cover them. The -x eye (under the sagging
  # cheek) sits lower — nothing about this face is level.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.054,0.046,0.102) r=0.026 wide=1.00 tall=0.90 deep=0.40 blend=0.005 color=241a15
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.054,0.044,0.079) r=0.017 wide=0.90 tall=0.90 deep=0.55 blend=0.004 color=d8cdb8 gloss=0.55
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.054,0.070,0.066) r=0.028 wide=1.05 tall=0.55 deep=0.70 blend=0.005
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(-0.050,0.038,0.106) r=0.024 wide=1.00 tall=0.90 deep=0.40 blend=0.005 color=241a15
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(-0.050,0.036,0.085) r=0.0155 wide=0.90 tall=0.90 deep=0.55 blend=0.004 color=d0c5b0 gloss=0.55
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(-0.050,0.061,0.078) r=0.026 wide=1.05 tall=0.55 deep=0.70 blend=0.005
  # (A crushed ear remnant was authored here and cut: on camera it read as a
  # black curled horn, which is worse than no ear at all.)

  # ============================================================
  # THE OVERGROWN ARM — the +x arm (side=l), directly under the swollen
  # shoulder and its second face. Every prim is side=l. The outline must
  # change: a deltoid twice the human arm's, a crooked knotted shaft, and a
  # forearm that runs PAST the wrist bone (to=1.75) so the oversized fist
  # hangs just above the knee line (fist bottom ~0.75, knee 0.555, hand bone
  # tail 1.18) — the bones stay human-length; the flesh is the verdict.
  # ============================================================
  # Deltoid: the biggest arm mass on the body, welded into the swollen
  # shoulder above it. `core`: the fuse probe's anchor.
  blob arm on clavicle at=1.00 r=0.175 blend=0.014 side=l core
  # Upper arm: a crooked heavy tube — the bend makes the knot visible in
  # silhouette, not just in surface. Girth is tuned against the chest wall
  # (a first draft at r 0.115 pressed the elbow into the chest and cost the
  # arm its daylight; the tilt=21 splay bought the air back for r 0.125).
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.02 to=0.95 r=0.125 r2=0.105 blend=0.012 bend=(0.045,-0.050,0.020) side=l
  # Knot: a swelling mid-shaft where the growth knotted.
  blob arm on upperArm at=0.55 offset=(0.022,-0.010,0.032) r=0.110 wide=1.05 tall=1.10 deep=1.05 blend=0.012 side=l
  # Elbow: a fused-looking knot, wider than the shafts it joins. Slimmer than
  # a first draft (r 0.110 / wide 1.15) which pressed the elbow INTO the
  # chest wall and cost the arm its daylight.
  blob arm on upperArm at=1.00 r=0.098 wide=1.05 tall=1.05 deep=1.05 blend=0.012 side=l
  # Forearm: thick, drooping, and LONG — the bar runs well past the wrist
  # bone, and the bend carries it forward-out so the fist clears the thigh.
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.10 to=1.75 r=0.118 r2=0.100 blend=0.010 bend=(0.060,0.030,0.035) side=l
  # Wrist knot above the fist: the "fused-looking" continue.
  blob arm on foreArm  at=1.60 r=0.112 wide=1.10 tall=1.05 deep=1.05 blend=0.010 side=l
  # OVERSIZED FIST: broader than tall, hung low (offset y -0.32 from the hand
  # bone's head region) ahead of the thigh.
  blob arm on hand     at=0.20 offset=(0.020,-0.320,0.040) r=0.170 wide=1.20 tall=0.85 deep=1.10 blend=0.010 side=l
  # Knuckle ridge: proud across the fist's front — reads knuckle-forward.
  bar  arm on hand     from=0.35 to=0.35 r=0.065 wide=1.30 tall=0.75 deep=0.90 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(0.020,-0.330,0.145) tip=(0,-0.020,0.020) side=l
  # Fused finger masses: two blunt rolls below the ridge, never separated
  # fingers — the fist fused into a club.
  bar  arm on hand     from=0.45 to=0.62 r=0.045 r2=0.032 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(0.075,-0.415,0.115) tip=(0.008,-0.045,0.020) side=l
  bar  arm on hand     from=0.45 to=0.62 r=0.043 r2=0.030 blend=0.005 chamfer offset=(-0.035,-0.415,0.110) tip=(-0.006,-0.045,0.018) side=l

  # ============================================================
  # THE HUMAN ARM — the -x arm (side=r): recognizably human, thick and
  # misshapen. One bulge on the forearm is the "misshapen"; everything else
  # is a heavy human arm that could one day close around a chainsaw grip.
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=0.95 r=0.095 blend=0.012 side=r core
  bar  arm on upperArm from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.072 r2=0.058 blend=0.008 side=r
  bar  arm on foreArm  from=0.05 to=0.92 r=0.060 r2=0.046 blend=0.008 side=r
  # The misshapen note: a bulge just below the outer elbow.
  blob arm on foreArm  at=0.42 offset=(-0.008,-0.008,0.014) r=0.056 wide=1.05 tall=1.10 deep=1.05 blend=0.008 side=r
  # Hand: a thick mitt with a stub of a thumb — grip-ready, not sculpted.
  blob arm on hand     at=0.50 r=0.060 wide=1.05 tall=0.65 deep=1.15 blend=0.008 side=r
  bar  arm on hand     from=0.75 to=1.00 r=0.018 r2=0.013 blend=0.004 offset=(-0.034,0.020,0.034) tip=(-0.012,-0.022,0.034) side=r

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — short, load-bearing pillars. Thick through the thigh, tapering to
  # a heavy ankle, into BROAD FLATTENED feet: wide, squat pads built for the
  # mass above them. No claws, no digitigrade geometry. The r1 legs were
  # sticks with ball joints; r2 fattens every segment and raises the blends
  # so knee and ankle read as fused weight-bearers, not beads.
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.05 r=0.170 blend=0.018 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.10 to=0.95 r=0.155 r2=0.125 deep=1.05 blend=0.018 mirror
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.05 to=0.90 r=0.115 r2=0.095 blend=0.016 mirror
  # Calf: a mass at the BACK of the shin, so the leg is a leg, not a peg.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.25 offset=(0,-0.005,-0.048) r=0.095 wide=1.00 tall=1.10 deep=0.90 blend=0.014 mirror
  # Ankle: heavy, fused-looking.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.98 r=0.090 wide=1.05 tall=0.95 deep=1.05 blend=0.014 mirror
  # FOOT: the broad flattened pad — wide in x, squat in y, long in z. Dropped
  # so the sole rests at y ~0.01.
  blob leg on foot  at=0.55 offset=(0,-0.008,0.020) r=0.105 wide=1.90 tall=0.50 deep=1.90 blend=0.012 mirror
  # Toes: one blunt wide mass closing the pad's front — flattened, not clawed.
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.95 to=1.05 r=0.058 wide=1.70 tall=0.50 deep=0.80 blend=0.006 chamfer offset=(0,-0.004,0.100) mirror

# Sheet block: a HAND-AUTHORED face decal (public/assets/lab/faces/
# sump-face.png, generated by scripts/make-sump-face.py) worn at MULTIPLY —
# the gargoyle road, third try. The head is small and same-colour SDF prims
# cannot budget it contrast: two geometry-only rounds read as a lumpy egg,
# and a first no-sheet-block draft painted two RED glowing zombie eyes just
# off the authored sockets (the registry-face path never sets eyeGlowCut, so
# the flat sheet's bright spots clear the 0.88 default cut). The decal is
# alpha-masked facial shading only — brow shadow, eye pits with a pale
# glint on the authored eyeballs, crushed-nose flanks, nasolabial folds,
# crooked mouth line, sagging -x cheek — over a neutral base normalised so
# the base luma equals the measured mean (base = no-op; only features
# deviate). Positions were derived in the cranium hs frame: the generator's
# hs() is the same (world - cranium centre) / semi-axes the shader projects.
# eyeGlowCut 0.99 + eyeGlowAmp 0 gate the sheet's glow off entirely (the
# white-sheet trap — nothing in this texture may glow; the PRD's eyes do not).
sheet
  image       sump-face.png
  decal       0
  projScaleX  0.19
  projScaleY  0.22
  projCentreX 0.50
  projCentreY 0.47
  eyeGlowCut  0.99
  eyeGlowAmp  0

# Face block: SHRUNK TO A NUB — the head is authored prims above (no reference
# mesh to bake; the generated sheet reads as the zombie). Same idiom as
# gnasher.blob and bloatmaw.blob.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006

# Sickly, thick and DULL. Waxy grey-beige base (near-equal channels, warm
# slightly); bruised plum mottle — hue-different from the base (r > b > g
# against a neutral base) so it reads as bruising IN the skin, not dirt ON
# it; raw red kept for wounds and the mouth interior. specRoughness high and
# wetness LOW — the shine lives on the painted mouth/seam prims, which carry
# their own gloss=. Translucency near zero (thick hide) — the r1 turntable
# rendered warmer/pinker than intended until this came down. Mottle amp 0.45
# lifts the mean toward the mottle, so the base sits a touch brighter to
# compensate.
palette
  baseColor     0.40 0.385 0.355
  deepColor     0.50 0.07 0.06
  charColor     0.06 0.05 0.04
  specIntensity 0.50
  specRoughness 0.55
  fresnelBoost  0.22
  translucency  0.06
  wetness       0.15
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.07
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.02
  mottleAmp     0.45
  mottleScale   1.6
  mottleColor   0.13 0.065 0.105
